[Music]  welcome to the QuickStart tutorial for  cloud functions we're going to see how  to deploy a cloud function from a Google  cloud project to start make sure you've  got a Google cloud project with building  enabled the first thing you'll want to  do is enable cloud functions API in the  navigation menu click on API and  services and click enable api's and  services here search for cloud functions  and select it from the results on the  cloud functions API page click enable to  enable it on the project next head to  cloud functions on navigation menu we'll  find this under the compute section  click here where it says create function  name your function whatever you'd like  for this demonstration we'll keep HTTP  selected as a trigger keep in line  editor selected for the source code as  we can see here cloud functions support  multiple runtimes for now we'll use  nodejs 8 by default we're provided with  a basic hello world function that will  respond to an HTTP request click on the  expanded editor window icon to get a  better look we won't have to make any  changes here so click OK  to go back here where it says function  to execute is where we would specify the  function in our source code that we'd  like to execute in this case HelloWorld  is the only one that we have and it's  the one that we want to execute click  create to deploy our cloud function the  cloud functions overview page will give  us a general overview of all of our  cloud functions including region trigger  run time and the time of its last  deployment as well as permissions once  it's done deploying click the menu of  our function and click test function on  the testing page we can test our  function by sending a triggering event  in JSON format our test function  responds to events by outputting the  value for a message so let's send it a  JSON object with a value 4 message click  on test the function and check out the  output  as we expected the function outputs the  message that we provided above down  below will see the log associated with  our function there are entries for when  the function execution started as well  as when the function finished along with  status code we can get an expanded view  of the logs by clicking here where it  says see all logs for this function  execution here we'll see the same log  entries along with a lot more  information should we need it and that's  all there is to it we've successfully  deployed a cloud function  [Music]

